From 7defd0666a523d57ec29169fc276670a459e8d2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eugene Flanagin <eflanagin@pm.me>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:15:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: (asus-ec-sensors) add TUF GAMING X870-PRO WIFI7 W NEO

Add support for the TUF GAMING X870-PRO WIFI7 W NEO. The board uses
the AMD 800-series EC register layout, and the ACPI mutex
\_SB_.PCI0.SBRG.SIO1.MUT0 exists in its DSDT, as on the other X870
boards.

The sensors were checked against other drivers on BIOS 1805 with a
Ryzen 7 7800X3D at idle and light desktop use:
 - CPU Package (0x31) follows k10temp Tctl within 1-2 degC
 - CPU (0x30) moves with Tctl, about 10 degC lower
 - Motherboard (0x32) equals the nct6799 SYSTIN reading
 - VRM (0x33) reads 39-42 degC at idle
 - CPU_Opt (0xb0) reads 520-1270 RPM and follows the CPU fan duty
   cycle, and matches none of the nct6799 fan inputs

T_Sensor is not added: with nothing plugged into the header, 0x36
reads 0 and 0x35 reads -62, so it could not be checked.

Signed-off-by: Eugene Flanagin <eflanagin@pm.me>
---
Notes (not part of the commit message):

On this board the EC bank register (0xff) was seen at 1 or 2 for periods
of a few seconds up to about two minutes, with no OS-side writer: it
happened with asus-ec-sensors unloaded and only ec_sys (write_support=0)
reading the EC. asus_ec_block_read() reads the bank first, warns about
concurrent access, switches to bank 0 and at the end writes the old
bank back through asus_ec_bank_switch(prev_bank, NULL), which writes
0xff on every poll even when nothing changed. That is unchanged by this
patch, but it means the driver and the firmware fight over the bank
register on this board. Happy to test a change to that logic.

ACPI DSDT (binary) for BIOS 1805 can be provided on request.

 Documentation/hwmon/asus_ec_sensors.rst |  1 +
 drivers/hwmon/asus-ec-sensors.c         | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/hwmon/asus_ec_sensors.rst b/Documentation/hwmon/asus_ec_sensors.rst
index 7032c40..364bdd8 100644
--- a/Documentation/hwmon/asus_ec_sensors.rst
+++ b/Documentation/hwmon/asus_ec_sensors.rst
@@ -66,6 +66,7 @@ Supported boards:
  * ROG ZENITH II EXTREME ALPHA
  * TUF GAMING X670E PLUS
  * TUF GAMING X670E PLUS WIFI
+ * TUF GAMING X870-PRO WIFI7 W NEO
 
 Authors:
     - Eugene Shalygin <eugene.shalygin@gmail.com>
diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/asus-ec-sensors.c b/drivers/hwmon/asus-ec-sensors.c
index 19f423e..3d06a9c 100644
--- a/drivers/hwmon/asus-ec-sensors.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/asus-ec-sensors.c
@@ -857,6 +857,14 @@ static const struct ec_board_info board_info_tuf_gaming_x670e_plus = {
 	.family = family_amd_600_series,
 };
 
+static const struct ec_board_info board_info_tuf_gaming_x870_pro_wifi7_w_neo = {
+	.sensors = SENSOR_TEMP_CPU | SENSOR_TEMP_CPU_PACKAGE |
+		SENSOR_TEMP_MB | SENSOR_TEMP_VRM |
+		SENSOR_FAN_CPU_OPT,
+	.mutex_path = ASUS_HW_ACCESS_MUTEX_SB_PCI0_SBRG_SIO1_MUT0,
+	.family = family_amd_800_series,
+};
+
 static const struct ec_board_info board_info_zenith_ii_extreme = {
 	.sensors = SENSOR_SET_TEMP_CHIPSET_CPU_MB | SENSOR_TEMP_T_SENSOR |
 		SENSOR_TEMP_VRM | SENSOR_SET_TEMP_WATER |
@@ -1004,6 +1012,8 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id dmi_table[] = {
 					&board_info_tuf_gaming_x670e_plus),
 	DMI_EXACT_MATCH_ASUS_BOARD_NAME("TUF GAMING X670E-PLUS WIFI",
 					&board_info_tuf_gaming_x670e_plus),
+	DMI_EXACT_MATCH_ASUS_BOARD_NAME("TUF GAMING X870-PRO WIFI7 W NEO",
+					&board_info_tuf_gaming_x870_pro_wifi7_w_neo),
 	{},
 };
 
